ADJUSTMENT OF RIGHTS AND OBLIGATIONS
The rights and obligations of the parties and their assignees upon a termination of a specified contract set out in the first column below (other than a specified contract that has become impossible of performance or been frustrated within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Frustrated Contracts Act (Cap. 115)) are adjusted in the manner set out opposite that contract in the second column below:
